<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT/PERIOD/DIRECTION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_combined/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Base color = wave height, exact bin colors (see table). Model height max this run: <b>11.3 ft</b>. Arrows point where the waves travel (WVDIR + 180&deg;). White halo numbers are the actual peak period at that spot (seconds between crests, e.g. 4.2s), drawn in the same style as the arrows and placed just above them; extra numbers mark spots where the period changes sharply even between arrows. Period max now <b>9.2s</b>, mean travel <b>151&deg; (SE)</b>. Significant height = average of highest third of waves.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — HTSGW height + PERPW peak period + WVDIR direction, surface analysis (single cycle)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT/PERIOD/DIRECTION — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Wave_Height_Period_Direction.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
